{"content":[{"c":["SHITTIM* (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Site on the plains of Moab where the Israelites made their final Transjordan encampment after defeating Sihon and Og (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.21-35","r":"Num.21.21-35","rawR":"Num.21.21-35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.21-35","value":"Num.21.21-35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:21-35"},") and prior to their crossing of the Jordan (",{"href":"?bref=Num.25.1","r":"Num.25.1","rawR":"Num.25.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.25.1","value":"Num.25.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:1"},"). According to ",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.49","r":"Num.33.49","rawR":"Num.33.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.49","value":"Num.33.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 33:49"},", this camp was near the Jordan, spreading from Beth-jeshimoth as far as Abel-shittim. Here Abel-shittim appears to be the full name of the place, while Shittim is the more common abbreviated toponym."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["At Shittim, Balak of Moab attempted to thwart the Israelite penetration of Canaan by hiring Balaam to curse the people of God (",{"href":"?bref=Num.22.1-24.25","r":"Num.22.1-24.25","rawR":"Num.22.1-24.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.22.1-24.25","value":"Num.22.1-24.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 22–24"},"), and later, apparently incited by Balaam’s counsel, Israel “played the harlot” with women from Midian and Moab (",{"href":"?bref=Num.25.1-5","r":"Num.25.1-5","rawR":"Num.25.1-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.25.1-5","value":"Num.25.1-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:1-5"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Num.31.15-16","r":"Num.31.15-16","rawR":"Num.31.15-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.31.15-16","value":"Num.31.15-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"31:15-16"},"). Israel’s apostasy, participating in idolatrous rites and engaging in ritual prostitution, was punished by Yahweh with the plague at Peor (",{"href":"?bref=Num.25.1-18","r":"Num.25.1-18","rawR":"Num.25.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.25.1-18","value":"Num.25.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 25:1-18"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.10.6-8","r":"1Cor.10.6-8","rawR":"1Cor.10.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.10.6-8","value":"1Cor.10.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 10:6-8"},"). Moses and Eleazar organized a census of the tribes while encamped at Shittim, and here Joshua was publicly proclaimed as Moses’ successor (",{"href":"?bref=Num.27.18-22","r":"Num.27.18-22","rawR":"Num.27.18-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.27.18-22","value":"Num.27.18-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 27:18-22"},"). Joshua dispatched two spies from Shittim to reconnoiter Jericho (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.2.1","r":"Josh.2.1","rawR":"Josh.2.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.2.1","value":"Josh.2.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 2:1"},"); later the Israelites prepared for the river crossing by breaking camp at Shittim and traveling to the Jordan (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.3.1","r":"Josh.3.1","rawR":"Josh.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.3.1","value":"Josh.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["Outside the Hexateuch the place-name Shittim occurs only in ",{"href":"?bref=Joel.3.18","r":"Joel.3.18","rawR":"Joel.3.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Joel.3.18","value":"Joel.3.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joel 3:18"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=Mic.6.5","r":"Mic.6.5","rawR":"Mic.6.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mic.6.5","value":"Mic.6.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Micah 6:5"},". The reference in Joel to the “valley of Shittim” or “wadi of the acacias” seems to be a symbol of barren aridity transformed into well-watered land when Yahweh restores his people in the eschaton, not a literal geographical location. Micah charges the people to remember “what happened from Shittim to Gilgal,” no doubt a reference to the crossing of the Jordan and the covenant promise of a land ultimately realized, as he recites the “saving acts” of Yahweh on Israel’s behalf."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ShittimPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 21:21-35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.21-35","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.21-35","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.21-35"},{"anchorText":"25:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.25.1","rawQueryValue":"Num.25.1","sourceRefExact":"Num.25.1"},{"anchorText":"Numbers 33:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.49","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.49","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.49"},{"anchorText":"Nm 22–24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.22.1-24.25","rawQueryValue":"Num.22.1-24.25","sourceRefExact":"Num.22.1-24.25"},{"anchorText":"25:1-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.25.1-5","rawQueryValue":"Num.25.1-5","sourceRefExact":"Num.25.1-5"},{"anchorText":"31:15-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.31.15-16","rawQueryValue":"Num.31.15-16","sourceRefExact":"Num.31.15-16"},{"anchorText":"Nm 25:1-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.25.1-18","rawQueryValue":"Num.25.1-18","sourceRefExact":"Num.25.1-18"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 10:6-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.10.6-8","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.10.6-8","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.10.6-8"},{"anchorText":"Nm 27:18-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.27.18-22","rawQueryValue":"Num.27.18-22","sourceRefExact":"Num.27.18-22"},{"anchorText":"Jos 2:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.2.1","rawQueryValue":"Josh.2.1","sourceRefExact":"Josh.2.1"},{"anchorText":"3:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.3.1","rawQueryValue":"Josh.3.1","sourceRefExact":"Josh.3.1"},{"anchorText":"Joel 3:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Joel.3.18","rawQueryValue":"Joel.3.18","sourceRefExact":"Joel.3.18"},{"anchorText":"Micah 6:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mic.6.5","rawQueryValue":"Mic.6.5","sourceRefExact":"Mic.6.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"87dc22243af78c8f219479475714ef557ccf4d67d6bd6fafb7a609ba4d95480c","sourceItemName":"ShittimPlace","sourceItemOrder":358,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ShittimPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shittim* (Place)","title":"Shittim* (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}